==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|fliohan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fleuhaną}}. Cognate with Dutch {{m|nl|vlieden}} and English {{m|en|flee}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|flieht|floh|geflohen|auxiliary=both}}

# {{label|de|intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[flee]]; to [[escape]]
# {{label|de|intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[diverge]]
#: ''Die Linien '''fliehen'''.'' — “The lines diverge.”
# {{label|de|transitive|auxiliary: “[[haben]]”}} to [[flee]] from (someone); to [[avoid]]

